# Site settings for the BIDS Apps Runner GUI. Copy to `site.env` (this repo's
# folder, gitignored) or to ~/.config/bids_apps_runner/site.env (yours alone;
# overrides the repo file). start_gui.sh reads it. Plain KEY=VALUE lines only --
# the file is never executed. An exported variable beats both files.
#
# Everything is optional. With nothing set, bulk data goes under YOUR scratch
# (/cl_tmp/<your user>/...) and the remote-DataLad features stay off.

# Where per-run bulk data lives (cohort logs, array scripts, subject lists,
# local dataset clones). Bulk data never goes under your home folder.
# Default: /cl_tmp/<your user>
#PRISM_SCRATCH_ROOT=/cl_tmp/yourname

# Remote DataLad server holding the datasets. The host must be a Host entry
# in your ~/.ssh/config (it carries the User/IdentityFile; a bare hostname
# does not work non-interactively). Both are needed to enable "Remote (SSH)"
# datasets and cohort setup/submit.
#PRISM_REMOTE_SSH_HOST=datalad-server
#PRISM_REMOTE_BASE_PATH=/datalad/mri/Your_Repository

# Where remote studies are cloned locally. Default: $PRISM_SCRATCH_ROOT/datasets
# (a shared lab folder is fine here, e.g. /cl_tmp/mrilab).
#PRISM_LOCAL_DATASET_BASE_DIR=/cl_tmp/yourname/datasets

# Cohort logs / generated scripts. Default:
# $PRISM_SCRATCH_ROOT/bids_apps_runner_cohort_logs
#PRISM_COHORT_LOG_BASE_DIR=/cl_tmp/yourname/bids_apps_runner_cohort_logs

# Where the GUI keeps its projects, settings and secret key. Default: your own
# ~/.bids_apps_runner (or this checkout, if it already holds your projects/).
# Never shared between users.
#PRISM_DATA_DIR=/home/yourname/.bids_apps_runner
